            "title": "Alcoa Stock Rises After Company Says Aluminum Pricing Is Offsetting Tariffs",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Shares of Alcoa were higher Thursday, a day after the company posted higher third-quarter sales and profit, and said that the delivery fee buyers pay for its aluminum from Canada is now more than offsetting tariff rates.  The company said the Midwest Premium, an additional cost added to the base price of aluminum delivered to the Midwest U.S., is now at 84 cents per pound of aluminum, which is covering the cost of the U.S.'s 50% tariff on aluminum imports.",
